course: dictionary
lesson: 80
title: What is an activator?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An activator is something that starts something working, or makes it more active. Think of it as a switch: it gets a change going.
explain: In science, an activator is a substance that starts or speeds up a chemical change. Some glues need one, like the hardener in some glues. Look at the word parts: activate means to make something start, so an activator is the thing that does the starting.
explain: Context gives clues. «Some slime recipes use activators that can make skin red and sore.» The sentence tells you an activator is a strong substance, not a toy, so it must be handled with care. Always check the sentence: does your meaning still make sense when you put it in?
fact: An activator is something that starts something working or makes it more active.
fact: In science, an activator starts or speeds up a chemical change.
fact: Some glues use an activator, such as a hardener, to set.
fact: «Some slime recipes use activators that can make skin red and sore.» So an adult should help, and hands should be washed afterwards.
fact: Phrases you may see on labels include glue activator and activator solution.
exercise: What is an activator? | A type of cloud | A kind of musical note | *Something that starts something working | A wet, muddy path
exercise: «Some slime recipes use activators that can make skin red and sore.» What does this tell you? | Activators make skin smooth and healthy | *Activators can irritate skin, so they need care | Activators are only found in toys | Activators are always safe to eat
exercise: Which phrase names a product you might find on a glue bottle? | *Glue activator | Soft toy | Wet wipe | Bubble bath
test: In science, what does an activator start or speed up? | A song | A walk in the park | *A chemical change | A bicycle ride
test: Why should an adult help make slime with an activator? | *Because activators can make skin red and sore | Because activators make hands cold | Because adults like slime more | Because slime is good to eat
exam: Which sentence uses the word activator correctly? | I drank an activator with my lunch | *The glue needed an activator to start setting | The dog's activator is brown and fluffy | The activator sang a song at the party
